	(gr_text "E-ink panel 29.2x59.2 (assumed position)"
		(at 131.9 145.8 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "ac499b45-6b5e-454c-96c9-c95b048257d3")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.6 0.6)
				(thickness 0.12)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "**Habits for routing this stackup:**\n\n1. **Route power as a star from the source.** \nRun +3V0 from the nPM2100 output caps (0.4 mm Power class) to each branch: \nRAK811, sensors, display. Give the RAK811 its own branch, \nbecause its ~130 mA TX bursts would otherwise shift the sensor supply.\n\n2. **Keep the switching loops tight on F.Cu.** The nPM2100 boost loop \n(VBAT → L1 → BOOST_SW → output caps → GND) and the display pump loop \n(DISP_SW → D3 → caps) should be as small as you can make them. \nPut their GND vias right at the cap pads so current drops straight into In1.\n Don't route anything else under L1 or L2.\n\n3. **Put the RF feed only on F.Cu over solid In1.** Use 0.371 mm track with a 0.2 mm \ngap, no vias, and no layer changes. Put GND vias on both sides at about 2 mm pitch, \nand one next to the U.FL ground pads and the RAK811 RF ground pin. \nKeep In1 unbroken under it.\n\n4. **Place a GND via at each decoupling cap's ground pad,** and keep the \ntrace from the cap to the IC's power pin short, with the cap between the \nvia and the pin.\n\n5. **Stitch ground everywhere.** Pour GND on both F.Cu and B.Cu. Stitch roughly \nevery 5 mm across the board and every 2 mm along the edges and around the RF. \nRemove any piece of pour with only one via.\n\n6. **Add a GND via beside every signal via.** With GND on both inner layers \nthis is cheap, and it keeps return currents short.\n\n7. **Treat In1 and In2 as planes, not routing layers.** If you have to route \non one, use In2, keep the trace short, and never pass under the RF feed. Also\n check that the via clearances don't cut a slot through the plane where several \nvias sit in a row, such as under J2's 24 pins.\n\n8. **Keep traces out of the SHT45 thermal slot.** Run only its four signals in, \nas thin traces (0.15 mm), so heat from the rest of the board doesn't reach the sensor.\n\n9. **Use 0.2 mm spacing on the ±20 V display traces** (the Display_HV class does this). \nKeep them away from the I2C and sensor lines.\n\n10. **Refill zones (B) before every DRC,** or DRC reports errors from the stale fill."
		(at 164.5 135 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "c157d2b0-6cc8-4956-b3aa-e5919fa5e901")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
